<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Tests for the Godot client (#190). A plain `Microsoft.NET.Sdk` project, not a
    `Godot.NET.Sdk` one. This assembly is run by `dotnet test`, never by the engine.

    **What is reachable from here, measured rather than assumed.** Godot's *managed*
    value types (`Color`, `Vector2`, `Rect2I` and the enums) are ordinary structs in
    `GodotSharp.dll` and work anywhere. Types deriving from `GodotObject`/`RefCounted`
    (`Image`, `Texture2D`, `InputEventKey`) are handles onto native objects: constructing
    one outside a running engine does not throw an exception a test can catch, it
    **terminates the test host process**, taking every other test in the run with it. A
    type deriving from `Node` can still have its *static* members called, because the
    type loads and its static fields initialise; that is what lets
    `FightScreen.ScaleFor` be tested without a screen.

    So the boundary this project holds to is: pure rules over managed types. Anything
    needing a live scene (drawing, input, `SpriteLibrary.Load`'s file reading, a whole
    turn played through `PlayMode`) stays with the client's own probe loop, which is a
    real Godot process.

    **The Godot source generators are removed below, deliberately.** Referencing the
    viewer pulls them in transitively, and they are written for a Godot project: one
    fails the build outright without `GodotProjectDir`, and another emits an entry point
    that collides by name with the client's own `Main`. Neither has anything to
    contribute to a test assembly (there are no `Node`-derived scripts here), so the
    right answer is to take them out rather than to feed them a made-up project
    directory. `GodotSharp.dll` itself is referenced as normal, which is all these tests
    need.

    **No content is loaded.** Every fixture is hand-authored, so this assembly adds
    nothing to the 27 corpus loads #319 is about, and needs no `RepositoryPaths`: it is
    not a fourth copy of the one #318 wants to consolidate.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="coverlet.collector" Version="6.0.4" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="18.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="3.1.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\client\SRDCombat.Viewer.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="RemoveGodotSourceGenerators" BeforeTargets="CoreCompile">
    <ItemGroup>
      <Analyzer Remove="@(Analyzer)" Condition="'%(Analyzer.Filename)' == 'Godot.SourceGenerators'" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
